Subject: [PATCH 11070/11362] State the print-your-population rule, and
 un-stall the doc/YAML table

Two things the hourly audit turned up.

The doc/YAML table was stale by two points: 611 and 612 were both reported in
hourly checks and never added, which is how a running table quietly stops
running. Both clean at 12, making five clean at 12 against three divergent at 14
across eight milestones, still with no counterexample and no 13-task plan to
locate the boundary.

The larger item is a rule I have applied three times in two days without ever
writing down. A check that finds nothing and a check that cannot find anything
produce identical output, and there is no way to tell them apart from outside.
arc_levelup_guarantee_lint could not fail for 21 of 59 milestones and reported
compliance throughout. My own corpus scan was guarded on a hasattr that is False,
measured zero artifacts, and would have been reported as "no other instances" if
the shape of the zero had not looked wrong. The QA-layer audit's entire
SILENT_NON_FIRING class exists for this and seven such findings currently stand.

So: every check prints what it examined, not only what it found. The two checks
built today do it, which is why this hour's clean cascade result was readable as
clean rather than as possibly-inert. When reading a green check that does not say
what it examined, you have not learned anything is clean, only that it said
nothing.

Left as prose rather than mechanised on purpose: a lint requiring a population
line would be pattern-matching over checker source, which is the same bug class
one level up. The three incidents are attached so the cost stays visible.

